# What an sdist must carry BEYOND the package itself.
#
# `packaging/macos/` is the macOS key agent's build input: the helper's C source, its
# Info.plist, the entitlements file, the bundle assembly script and the wheel retag.
# It is not package code — nothing in `local_operator/` imports it — but it is the
# only way to BUILD the signed helper, and CI builds the macOS wheel from the wheel
# rather than from this tree. Without this line an sdist would ship a package whose
# macOS presence tier cannot be built by anyone who has the sdist but not the
# repository, which is the opposite of "the build inputs are public, the signed
# output is not committed" (docs/design/operator-key-agent.md §7).
#
# The signed artefact itself is never in an sdist or a wheel built from source: it
# cannot be, since it needs the signing identity and the profile.
graft packaging/macos
